402:#  *** THIS IS **THE** ACCEPT ROW FOR THE TICK, not merely a neighbour: the write to imask0 is
403:#  precisely what used to ARM the host death at :78, so it is the predicate that gated death. ***
404:#  *** THE SENTENCE THAT STOOD HERE WAS MEASURED FALSE THE SAME DAY.  It read: "Safe under
405:#  `step' ONLY: tickshift is 16, so the tick fires every 65536 cycles and a handful of steps
406:#  cannot reach it."  A HANDFUL OF STEPS REACHES IT ON THE FIRST ONE. ***
407:#  `machine_add_tickfunction' sets `ticks_till_next[n] = 0' (machine.c:354) while
408:#  `ticks_reset_value[n] = 1 << tickshift' (:355), and `machine_run()' decrements then fires
409:#  while <= 0 -- so THE FIRST machine_run OF ANY SESSION FIRES EVERY TICK FUNCTION.
410:#  THIS ROW IS STILL SAFE -- BUT ONLY ONE OF THE TWO REASONS BELOW IS LOAD-BEARING, AND
411:#  SAYING OTHERWISE INVERTS A HAZARD INTO A SAFETY PROPERTY (Fable adjudication, same day):
412:#  *** REASON (2) MISDIRECTS.  This row's value is 1<<18 = 0x40000, which has NO high bits
413:#  at ANY store width -- so width is irrelevant to THIS row, and reason (1) alone carries
414:#  it.  Written as a pair, `sw cannot set bit 50' reads as a general safety invariant for
415:#  imask0, AND IT IS NOT ONE: THE DEATH IS REACHABLE, BY `sd 1<<50'. ***
416:#  Keep both facts, but know which is which: (1) is why this row is safe; (2) is why a
417:#  COPY of it would be inert as a kill row.  They are a safety reason and a HAZARD.
418:#    (1) it writes bit 18, not bit 50, so the guarded branch is never armed; and
419:#    (2) *** IT USES `sw', AND A 4-BYTE STORE CANNOT SET BIT 50 AT ALL. ***  `case 0x10000'
420:#        does `d->imask0 = idata' with `idata = memory_readmax64(cpu, data, len)', so a
421:#        word store caps idata below 2^32.  ARMING THE TICK REQUIRES `sd' (0xFCE80000).
422:#  *** AND THAT IS A FALSE-GREEN TRAP FOR THE NEXT PERSON: `OP_SW_T0_A3' IS THE ONLY STORE
423:#  HELPER IN THIS FILE, so a tick row copy-pasted from here would arm NOTHING, stay ALIVE,
424:#  and score GREEN ON A LIVE HOST DEATH. ***  Measured: sw 0xffffffff + 70000 steps -> alive.
425:#  The tick witness lives in tick_20260917/ip30_tick_probe.py, which uses `sd'.
426:t, alive = session(guest_store(A_IMASK0, 1 << 18) + guest_load(A_IMASK0))
427:row("acc imask", (printed(t, "v0") if alive else "died"), "0x40000",
428:    "case 0x10000 (imask0) accepts and reads back. THE accept row for the tick predicate -- "
429:    "bit 18 is used, NOT bit 50, so the row does not arm the death it is pinning.")
