437:     "abort() -- corruption AND host death in one arm. ***"),
438:    ("kill 28 rd", A_CLRISR,
439:     "case 0x10028, same missing writeflag test; `d->isr &= ~idata' is a no-op at idata==0, "
440:     "then abort()."),
441:):
442:    t, alive = session(guest_load(addr))
443:    row(nm, ("alive" if alive else "DEAD"), "alive", note)
444:    #  *** RE-PINNED 2026-09-17 ONTO THE SHIPPED #531 TEXT.  The old literal was the
445:    #  PRE-FIX message `IP30 legacy interrupt rewrite: TODO', which #531 replaces with a
446:    #  latched announce -- so this row pinned a string the fix legitimately renames.
447:    #  ORDER DISCRIMINATOR (the oracle-correction rule): the re-pin is shown RED on a
448:    #  PRE-FIX binary before being trusted -- see artifacts/ip30abortkill/REPIN_*.out.
449:    #  *** WANT "no" SINCE 2026-09-18: the read arms adopted MEMBER 2, SILENT DECLINE, on the
450:    #  fable5 ruling.  These rows previously wanted "yes" and pinned an announce that was a
451:    #  FALSE MESSAGE (a read is not a rewrite) and a BIT THIEF (one benign read consumed the
452:    #  shared IP30_W_ISR latch and silenced the genuine write-side diagnostic for the device's
453:    #  life).  They now pin the SILENCE, which is the repair's own observable. ***
454:    row(nm + " txt", ("yes" if "sgi_ip30: interrupt-status rewrite not implemented" in t else "no"), "no",
455:        "DIAGNOSIS ONLY, never half the trigger: a reworded-message mutant still abort()s, "
456:        "gives EOF with no text, and an EOF-AND-text oracle would certify it GREEN.")
